course: dictionary
lesson: 14637
title: Preacher: two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A preacher is a person who gives religious talks, called sermons, usually in a church. «The preacher spoke for twenty minutes about kindness to strangers.» The context tells you the word is about church, so this is the first meaning.
explain: Read the words around a word to choose its meaning. «Stop being such a preacher, Ella!» Ella is not in a church. Her friend is telling her how to behave, and that is the second meaning. It is informal and a bit negative.
explain: Some phrases use preach too. «Practise what you preach» means do the things you tell other people to do. «Preaching to the choir» means telling people what they already agree with, so the talk does no real persuading.
fact: A preacher is a person who gives religious talks, called sermons.
fact: In informal talk, a preacher is someone who keeps telling others how they should behave.
fact: «Preachy» describes someone who lectures others about right and wrong.
fact: «Preaching to the choir» means telling people what they already agree with.
fact: «Practise what you preach» means do the things you tell others to do.
exercise: «The preacher spoke to the crowd outside the church.» What is a preacher? | A person who sells train tickets | A pet that barks at strangers | A tall building with a bell | *A person who gives religious talks
exercise: «Stop being such a preacher, Ella!» What does preacher mean here? | A person who gives religious talks in a church | A loud singer | *Someone who keeps telling others how to behave | A kind teacher who helps at lunchtime
exercise: Which phrase means telling people what they already agree with? | Practise what you preach | Quiet as a mouse | *Preaching to the choir | Lay preacher
test: «Every Sunday the preacher reads from an old book.» Where would you most likely hear a preacher? | *In a church | In a swimming pool | On a bus | At a football match
test: Which word describes someone who lectures others about right and wrong? | *Preachy | Shy | Tidy | Hungry
exam: «Ben said, "Practise what you preach, Dad!" when his dad kept shouting about shouting.» What does practise what you preach mean? | Keep your hands clean | Preach loudly in a church | *Do the things you tell others to do | Sing in the church choir
